<https://github.com/corrado877/CognitiveBiasOntologies/blob/main/HotHandFallacyOntology/HotHandFallacyOntology.owl#ProbabilityLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The probability level that an event n the next futur, such a chance-based occurence, can have  a specific outcome effect. For example In the Hot Hand fallacy bias if the outcome of previous events series was a Victory then for the player the probability level that the next  event will be a Victory is higher. On the contrary in the opposite bias, the stock of luck, the player belevies that is less probable of winning again in the next event because the luck will be less." .
